{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\sci\\042.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "4.1DIGESTION", "conf": 0.897, "box": [[87, 51], [369, 51], [369, 87], [87, 87]]}, {"text": "Imagine you have just eaten an apple. Can your body absorb the nutrients of apple directly", "conf": 0.916, "box": [[80, 108], [1199, 114], [1199, 159], [79, 154]]}, {"text": "aftereating?", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[85, 163], [245, 163], [245, 200], [85, 200]]}, {"text": "You just learned that your food mainly consists of large molecules of carbohydrates,", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[85, 219], [1217, 223], [1217, 263], [84, 259]]}, {"text": "proteins and fats. These molecules are too big to enter your cells through cell membrane.", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[85, 269], [1200, 270], [1200, 307], [85, 306]]}, {"text": "Your body cells cannot use food until it is broken down into smaller molecules.Digestion is", "conf": 0.918, "box": [[87, 314], [1195, 317], [1195, 353], [86, 350]]}, {"text": "thebreakdownoffoodintosmallermolecules.", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[87, 362], [638, 362], [638, 392], [87, 392]]}, {"text": "Digestion begins as soon as you chew thefood. It continues as the food travels through the", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[87, 418], [1191, 418], [1191, 454], [87, 454]]}, {"text": "organs of the digestive system. Food breakdown starts with physical digestion. The large", "conf": 0.902, "box": [[84, 464], [1191, 465], [1191, 501], [84, 500]]}, {"text": "pieces of food are broken into smaller pieces by cutting and chewing action of your teeth.", "conf": 0.941, "box": [[86, 510], [1190, 508], [1190, 543], [86, 546]]}, {"text": "Your tongue also helps by mixing and rolling of food. The muscles of your stomach help in", "conf": 0.922, "box": [[87, 554], [1191, 553], [1191, 589], [87, 590]]}, {"text": "mechanicaldigestion.", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[89, 601], [350, 601], [350, 634], [89, 634]]}, {"text": "Activity4.1PhysicalDigestion", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[109, 678], [574, 676], [574, 719], [109, 721]]}, {"text": "Take